# Build a Twilight Huntsman and photograph the three things bd inc-tek.8.3
# changed about that class: its spell access (PA-03-F1), the target of its
# Smite (PA-03-F2) and the rate its Tracking advances (PA-03-F19).
#
# WHY A CHARACTER IS NEEDED. All three fixes are grants in the class's Grants:
# block. A grant does nothing until somebody holds the class, so reading the
# class description -- which is all tools/keys/prestige-tables.keys does --
# cannot see any of them. The character sheet reports all three:
#   "Smite Lawful Creatures"    src/Sheet.cpp:501-509
#   "Tracking (280 feet)"       src/Sheet.cpp:719, AbilityLevel(CA_TRACKING)*10
#   the [L]earn Spells menu     src/Create.cpp:4190-4198 builds it from the
#                               SPELL_ACCESS stati this fix added
#
# THE BUILD, and why it is a multiclass. The class wants Ride 8, Athletics 8,
# Hide 5, Animal Empathy 5, Move Silently 5 and Maeve as patron
# (lib/prestige.irh:2802-2818). No single class covers those five skills:
# Character::MaxRanks (src/Create.cpp:3600-3629) allows ranks only in a skill
# one of your classes carries, so a skill no class of yours has is capped at
# zero ranks and can never be raised. The ranger has Animal Empathy and the
# rogue has Athletics; neither has both. Hence Ranger 3 / Rogue 3, which is
# also the cheapest total: ranks are capped by the levels of the classes that
# carry the skill, and six levels buy nine ranks in a shared skill.
#
# An elf is given Maeve at birth (lib/races.irh:1144-1147), so no conversion
# is needed.
#
# SEED. The attribute rolls and the offered feats vary with the seed, so the
# feat picks stay positional and a seed is passed.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Elf"
@choose "Elf (Standard)"
@choose "Ranger"
a                       # Attributes: the first of the offered sets
@choose "Neutral"
@choose "Goblinkin"     # favoured enemy. Goblinkin are the early-dungeon
                        #   staple and they are Lawful, so this is also the
                        #   creature type the corrected Smite now bites.
a                       # Combat style: [a] archery
@until "Unspent Skill Ranks" a          # however many feats are asked for

# Twelve ranks, two to a skill, in the ranger list. Athletics cannot be
# bought here -- the ranger does not carry it, so its cap is zero until the
# rogue levels arrive.
@cursorto:mark "Animal Empathy" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Hide in Shadows" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Move Silently" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Ride" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Searching" DOWN
RIGHT*2
@cursorto:mark "Listen" UP
RIGHT*2
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

a       # Personality archetype

ESC     # dismiss the arrival-room description; now in play
w       # wizard mode
y       # "Enter wizard mode?" -- yes
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
DOWN DOWN
SPACE   # Free Advancement: NO -> YES
ESC

d       # character sheet
M       # [M]ulticlass
@choose "Rogue"

# Five levels: three rogue, two ranger, reaching Ranger 3 / Rogue 3.
# @until presses G through whatever the level-up asks first; @choose answers
# the class question by name; @while clears a feat menu when one appears.
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Rogue"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Rogue"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Rogue"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Ranger"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Ranger"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@expect "Ranger 3"

# Ride to its cap in the ranger view, then TAB to the rogue view for
# Athletics. The Skill Manager keeps one pool and one list per class.
S
@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
@cursorto:mark "Ride" DOWN
RIGHT*7
TAB
@cursorto:mark "Athletics" DOWN
RIGHT*6
ENTER y

P                               # [P]restige Classes
@expect "Choose a class:"
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@expect "Huntsman 0"            # the gate let him in

# Five huntsman levels. Smite arrives at 3rd, Scent at 5th, and Tracking
# has had three of its +2 steps by then.
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@until "class do you wish to advance" G
@choose "Twilight Huntsman"
@while "Choose a feat" a
@expect "Huntsman 5"

W                       # Write Dump
h u n t ENTER           # filename: "hunt"

L                       # [L]earn Spells -- the spell list oracle
@dump:learn
ESC
ESC
@quit
